# ── Run outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `artifacts/runs/` is tracked ON PURPOSE: it holds the per-cell results the paper's tables are
# read back from (summary json, per-client report.json, and the score profiles the fusion
# analysis consumes). What a NEW run adds to that tree is not tracked -- checkpoints, token
# caches and loss histories are gigabytes and reproduce from the code.
#
# `artifacts/*` and not `artifacts/`: git never descends into an ignored DIRECTORY, so with the
# plain form the re-inclusion on the next line would never be reached. Everything else under
# artifacts/ -- a smoke tree, a scratch tag -- is still ignored.
#
# Under artifacts/runs/ only the PUBLISHED tags are re-included, one by one (the list is appended
# below when the tree is exported). A tag you produce yourself therefore stays untracked by
# default: your runs are yours, and they cannot be committed by an absent-minded `git add -A`.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/runs/
artifacts/runs/*
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
all_time_series_train_test_all_features/
fed_history.json
knobs.json
placement.tsv

logs/
plots/

# Datasets: downloaded and built locally, never committed. NB: no trailing slash on the
# archive path -- with one, `git add` still tracks a SYMLINK left there by a local run.
data/
preprocessing/dataset/AnomalyDatasets_2021

